test_command=sh tests/antz-flow_test.sh && sh tests/orchestrator-status-probe_test.sh && sh tests/orchestrator-skills-block_test.sh && sh tests/orchestrator-render-sync_test.sh
id=testharness-01 result=green reason=tests/antz-flow_test.sh loads scripts/orchestration/antz-flow.sh (and the probe file for the state tests) as real files with no extraction step reading agents/prompts/orchestrator.prompt; the extraction helpers (extract_flow, the probe awk, the mktemp copies) are gone; every pre-existing flow assertion keeps passing unchanged against the file (26 pass, 1 e2e skip)
id=testharness-02 result=green reason=tests/orchestrator-status-probe_test.sh runs scripts/orchestration/antz-probe.sh directly with CHANGE_DIR pointed at fixture change dirs, no extraction from the prompt (extract_script gone); all pre-existing probe assertions keep passing unchanged, plus the suite's file-source guard checks sh -n, the shebang, and that the prompt's probe fence is exactly its include marker (20 pass, 0 fail)
id=testharness-03 result=green reason=tests/orchestrator-skills-block_test.sh runs scripts/orchestration/antz-skills.sh directly (marker-to-fence-close extractor gone, so the shebang first line the old extractor dropped is kept); every pre-existing block/derivation/matching/none-matched/constraint and body-never-read assertion passes unchanged; the orchestrator.prompt additive-vs-HEAD guard is re-scoped: each of the three script fences must carry exactly its "# antz-include:" marker line naming an existing file, and removed lines are permitted only inside those three fenced bodies (any removal outside them still fails, exercised by synthetic hunks on both diff sides plus the real tree's diff); the constraint test's sh -n now parses the file (11 pass, 2 e2e/transient skips)
id=testharness-04 result=green reason=new tests/orchestrator-render-sync_test.sh renders install.sh --all for both clients into an isolated temp HOME and compares each installed antz-orchestrator body's three script fences against the current scripts/orchestration/ files byte-for-byte with the fence indentation re-applied (cmp equality, sharing install.sh's one pinned antz-skills.sh carve-out); drift is mechanized: tampering one byte of one installed fence reports exactly that script out of sync, so a file change without a matching re-render fails the suite (2 pass, 0 fail)
